<p>
	Here is a small collection of games I made using <a href="https://www.construct.net/en/construct-2/download" target="_blank">Construct 2</a> back when I was newer to programming and game development. Metadata on the project files suggests they're all from 2018 but I'm inclined to believe these were made around 2016 or so. I don't intend to update or build on any of these, I provide them purely for historical interest.
</p>
<span class="hr-light"></span>
<p>
	Note: these games require keyboard input and are designed for PC devices.
</p>
<span class="hr-light"></span>
<p>
	<a href="/games/c2/antivirus">Antivirus</a>
	<br>
	A side-scrolling platformer/shooter. The levels quickly shift from actual gameplay to messing around.
</p>
<p>
	<a href="/games/c2/superTurretShooter">Super Turret Shooter</a>
	<br>
	A simple top-down shooter. There were experiments with switching between top-down and side-scrolling mid-level. Mouse input required for aiming and shooting.
</p>
<p>
	<a href="/games/c2/theOpenRoad">The Open Road</a>
	<br>
	Top-down racing game where you race against the clock. Features terrain that affects your speed. Mouse input required for menus.
</p>
<p>
	<a href="/games/c2/upag">Unnamed Pixel-Art Game</a>
	<br>
	A weird side-scrolling platformer thing. You get a grappling hook. Mouse input required for menus and the grappling hook.
</p>
<p>
	<a href="/games/c2/hyperMarble">HyperMarble</a>
	<br>
	Side-scrolling marble game. Has a basic layer system for things like shuttle loops.
</p>
